Title: Design Intern &nbsp;

Role Overview &nbsp;

You will play a crucial role in providing support to the Creative team with exploring and conceptualising design approaches and solutions across various projects that maintain the company’s vision and creative beliefs - ‘great ideas expertly and beautifully crafted and delivered with rigour and flair’. &nbsp;

Job Responsibilities &nbsp;

• Creative Conceptualization - Ideate &amp; collaborate with the Creative team to craft concepts that are inventive, and strategic, and create meaningful experiences for diverse industries and audiences.&nbsp; &nbsp;

• Visual Asset Design &amp; Support - Work collaboratively with multidisciplinary project teams to bring our client’s stories to life using communication design principles, including presentations, graphics, documents, and digital assets.&nbsp; &nbsp;

• Graphic Oversight - Ensure comprehensive project design and aid in execution through consistent coordination with the internal design team, and external design vendors.&nbsp; &nbsp;

• Graphic Production - Follow design systems and champion best practices to produce production-ready designs for digital, print, and retail applications. &nbsp;

&nbsp;

Experience Needed / Our Requirements &nbsp;

• Currently pursuing or recently completed a Bachelor's or Master's degree in Design. &nbsp;

• Proven ability to apply and perform graphic design skills, including ideation, drawing/sketching, typography, use of colour palettes and texture, and visual presentation development.&nbsp; &nbsp;

• Ability to work across scale in digital, print, and physical spaces, from app icon design to wall murals. &nbsp;

• Ability to showcase ideas and concepts through different mediums from sketching, illustrating, motion, and creating mock-ups.&nbsp; &nbsp;

• Prior experience in brand identity creation and/or experience in the application of the established visual guidelines. &nbsp;

• Demonstrate proficiency in Adobe Creative Suite (Illustrator, InDesign, Photoshop) and Figma.&nbsp; &nbsp;

• Basic motion and 3D design knowledge are an added advantage. &nbsp;

• Prior experience in environmental graphic design would be an advantage.&nbsp; &nbsp;

• Knowledge of and sensitivity to design trends and industry standards. &nbsp;

• Prior internship or work experience in a similar role would be an advantage. &nbsp;

