You will be responsible for:

• Assessing residents and providing specialist equipment, including non-standard stock items and moving and handling equipment.

• Assessing for minor and major home adaptations through Disabled Facilities Grants (DFGs).

• Working closely with internal departments and external organisations.

• Supporting residents to live safely and independently within their homes.

2.Occupational Therapist - Assistive Technology

You will be responsible for:

• Assessing residents for a range of assistive technology solutions.

• Supporting the assessment and review project within domiciliary care services.

• Identifying technology-enabled care solutions to support residents' independence and wellbeing.

• Working collaboratively with colleagues to ensure appropriate technology is implemented.

Benefits: &nbsp;

• £32.00 per hour

• Hybrid working - 3 days remote and 2 days in the office.

• Based at Churchill Court, 2 Westmoreland Road, Bromley, BR1 1AS.

